From: GT-BE19000AI kernel development
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] pidfd: backport process handles without changing vendor structs

Backport Linux v5.4 pidfd_open, pidfd_send_signal, CLONE_PIDFD and
waitid(P_PIDFD), including close-on-exec descriptors, poll notification,
process namespace checks, signal permissions and failure cleanup. Support
AArch64 and AArch32 using upstream syscall numbers 424 and 434.

Keep every struct pid/task_struct field unchanged for vendor modules.
Replace the upstream per-pid wait queue with 256 permanent hashed queues.
Hash collisions only produce spurious wakeups; readiness always checks the
referenced pid under RCU. All pidfd references retain struct pid so numeric
PID reuse cannot retarget a handle. No unsupported probe is faked.

Use the modern fdinfo Pid=-1 convention for reaped processes and NSpid.
This does not implement clone3, PIDFD_NONBLOCK, pidfd_getfd or pidfs ioctls.
Ubuntu systemd259/glibc2.43 can fall back to legacy clone(CLONE_PIDFD).

Source reference: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/tree/v5.4
Adaptations: 4.19 siginfo layout; static copy_process pidfd pointer;
unchanged exported fork APIs; cgroup cleanup ordering; hashed wait queues.

